<title>ITALY: Italy's Palermo sees Dec CPI at 1.8 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Italy's Palermo sees Dec CPI at 1.8 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>PALERMO, Italy 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Palermo said its December consumer price index stood at 0.1 percent month-on-month and 1.8 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>In November, Palermo's inflation rate was 0.1 percent and 1.8 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Palermo is one of 10 Italian cities publishing inflation data on Thursday and Friday.</p>
<p>The city's CPI has a weighting of 6.80 percent on the national index. The 10 sample cities have a combined weighting of 69.67 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to November 1996):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		     0.1   (0.1)     1.8  (1.8)</p>
<p>    Food				  0.0  (-0.1)     3.3  (3.6)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	   0.0   (0.0)     1.9  (2.0)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges   0.2   (1.2)     0.6  (0.4)</p>
<p>    Furniture			  -0.5   (0.2)     0.9  (1.6)</p>
<p>    Health services		   0.0   (0.0)     2.0  (1.8)</p>
<p>    Transportation		    0.1   (0.5)     2.4  (2.4)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture     0.4   (0.1)     0.4  (0.0)</p>
<p>    Education			   0.9   (0.0)     0.2 (-0.7)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	  0.0  (-0.2)     1.6  (1.6)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	 0.1  (-0.3)    -0.2 (-0.3)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129526</p>
